# Mobile-First Responsive Design

Every new feature, section, page, or component must be designed for mobile first, then enhanced for larger screens.

## Rules

- Unprefixed Tailwind classes target the smallest screen (~320px). Add `xs:` (480px), `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` only to scale *up*.
- Never write desktop styles first and undo them with smaller breakpoints. Do not use `max-*:` variants unless there is no alternative.
- Layouts start as a single column (`flex-col` / `grid-cols-1`) and gain columns at larger breakpoints.
- No fixed pixel widths on containers. Use `w-full`, `max-w-*`, and fluid padding (`px-5 md:px-10`).
- No horizontal overflow at 320px. Long words/URLs need `break-words`; wide content needs `overflow-x-auto`.
- Tap targets are at least 44×44px (`min-h-11 min-w-11`) with adequate spacing.
- Use the fluid `text-display-*` sizes for headings; body text is never below `text-sm`.
- Hover-only interactions must have a tap/focus equivalent. Navigation must work on mobile (menu toggle).
- Images use `w-full h-auto` or `object-cover` with an aspect ratio, and `loading="lazy"` below the fold.
- Prefer `min-h-svh` over `h-screen` for full-height mobile sections.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: desktop-first, fixed width, overflows on phones
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-12 w-[1200px] max-md:grid-cols-1">

// ✅ GOOD: mobile-first, fluid, scales up
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-12 w-full max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-10">
```

## Before Finishing a Feature

Check the layout at 320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px, and 1440px. Confirm there is no horizontal scroll, text is readable, and every interactive element is reachable by touch.
